{"author": "pgaudet", "body": "Hello, \n\nBecause we didn't used to have checks on the prefixes allowed in Noctua, some bad data has creeped in: \nsee https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1DE6NbDCULf3Dds5iyDErENwKzvFEJULuUmranM-T58E/edit?gid=0#gid=0\n\nUnfortunately these cannot be fixed automatically, due to \n1.  no mapping found (for GenBank, EMBL, etc) - we have already mapped all we could from those)\n2. Errors too rare to make a useful rule. \n\n \n<google-sheets-html-origin><style type=\"text/css\"><!--td {border: 1px solid #cccccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\nAssigned by |  \n-- | --\nBHF-UCL | 1\nFlyBase | 1 DONE\nMGI | 138 DONE\n~PomBase | 5~ DONE\nSGD | 6\nUniProt | 39\nWB | 27\nXenbase | 5\nZFIN | 45\n\n\nMoving forward, since we have a limited set of prefixes curators can use, we expect these errors not to occur again. \n\nThanks, Pascale", "created_at": "2025-12-01T17:41:40Z", "key": "issue", "labels": [], "state": "open", "state_reason": "reopened", "title": "Noctua data to be manually corrected", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2026-02-09T09:00:20Z"}
